#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:4
msgid ""
"Every logged-in player can write achievements for a game on the site. A new "
"achievement starts unofficial: it is never awarded, so you can test it in "
"the emulator before it counts for anyone."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:9
msgid "From unofficial to official"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:12
msgid "Open the editor"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:13
msgid ""
"Log in, open the game's page and press New achievement. The editor asks for "
"a title, a description, the points, the type, a badge image, the condition "
"and the status."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:14
msgid "See the games →"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:17
msgid "Write the condition"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:18
msgid ""
"The condition (mem_addr) tells the emulator which memory values unlock the "
"achievement. The syntax is the same as on RetroAchievements; the pointers "
"below cover the basics."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:21
msgid "Save it unofficial"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:22
msgid ""
"On save, the editor checks the condition with the same rcheevos parser the "
"emulators run and refuses a malformed one, showing the parser's reason. A "
"condition that parses can still be wrong: only the game proves it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:25
msgid "Test it in DuckStation"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:26
msgid ""
"Log in to DuckStation, turn on Test Unofficial Achievements in Settings → "
"Achievements, then close the game and open it again: the emulator only "
"fetches the achievements when a game loads."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:27
msgid ""
"Unofficial achievements appear in the achievement list marked (Unofficial); "
"the pause screen's counter only counts official ones. The pop-up fires when "
"the condition is met, which proves it works, but an unofficial achievement "
"is never recorded or worth points."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:28
msgid ""
"An achievement of a bonus or challenge subset loads only after you turn on "
"Play this subset in that subset's section of the game page."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:31
#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:42
msgid "Make it official"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:32
msgid ""
"Back in the editor, set the status to Official. Every player then receives "
"it as an official achievement, and unlocking it counts and scores."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:33
msgid "What each status means →"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:39
#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:71
msgid "Condition syntax"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:40
msgid ""
"A condition compares memory values. These are the pieces most conditions use:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:44
msgid ""
"The 8-bit value at address 0x1234. 0x is 16-bit, 0xW 24-bit and 0xX 32-bit; "
"0xM to 0xT read single bits."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:48
msgid "The delta: the value the address held on the previous frame."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:52
msgid "Joins conditions: all of them must be true on the same frame."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:56
msgid ""
"Starts an alternative group: the core conditions plus any one group must be "
"true."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:60
msgid ""
"Flags before a condition: ResetIf clears every hit count when it is true, "
"PauseIf suspends the check while it is true."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:64
msgid ""
"A hit count after a condition: it must be true on that many frames before it "
"counts."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:67
msgid ""
"For example, this condition fires on the frame the byte at 0x61998 changes "
"from 0 to 1:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:69
msgid ""
"RetroAchievements' developer documentation covers every size, prefix and "
"flag:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:72
msgid "Why delta"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:73
msgid "Hit counts"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:75
msgid "Alt groups"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:76
msgid "All developer docs"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:81
msgid "Good practices"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:83
msgid ""
"Describe the moment something happens, not a state: compare the value with "
"its delta, as in the example above. A plain comparison can be true for a "
"frame while the game boots and unlock the achievement on load."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:84
msgid ""
"Console memory is zeroed at reset, so a 0 often means the game is not "
"running yet. Guard the condition with a value that is only non-zero during "
"play, such as a pointer."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:85
msgid ""
"The emulator holds back an achievement whose condition is already true when "
"the game loads. Test from a save state made before the moment it should fire."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:86
msgid ""
"Check each address you rely on: code notes describe what the community "
"found, often on another region of the game."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/creating-achievements.html:87
msgid ""
"Every save keeps a revision. The History link on the game page shows them, "
"and the author or staff can revert to one."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:4
msgid "Short answers to what players and authors ask most."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:9
msgid "Which discs are supported?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:10
msgid ""
"The emulator recognises a game by a hash of its disc: for PlayStation, the "
"hash of the boot executable named in SYSTEM.CNF. A disc only gets "
"achievements when its hash is registered for a game here, so another region "
"or revision of the same game, with a different executable, is not recognised."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:22
msgid "No disc registered yet"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:28
msgid "Why did an achievement not unlock?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:30
msgid ""
"The emulator did not recognise the disc, so it loaded no achievements for "
"it. Check that your disc is in the list above."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:31
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The emulator is not connected to this site: check the Host in DuckStation's "
"settings.ini and that you are logged in, as the <a href=\"%(start_url)s\" "
"class=\"text-brand\">getting started guide</a> shows."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:32
msgid ""
"It is unofficial: the emulator lists it only with Test Unofficial "
"Achievements on, and an unofficial achievement is never recorded or worth "
"points."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:33
msgid ""
"Its condition was already true when the game loaded, for example from a save "
"state made after the moment: the emulator holds it back until the condition "
"turns false and true again."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:34
msgid ""
"It changed after you opened the game: the emulator only fetches achievements "
"when a game loads, so close the game and open it again."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:35
msgid ""
"It has a bug. Tell its author in the comments on the achievement's page."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:40
msgid "Hardcore or softcore?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:41
msgid ""
"Both are worth the same points, and the site shows each total apart. "
"Hardcore turns off save states, cheats and rewind; an achievement unlocked "
"in hardcore also counts in softcore. Leaderboards only run in hardcore."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:45
msgid "Do I need a RetroAchievements account?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:46
msgid ""
"No. RetroPlatinas speaks the same protocol as RetroAchievements, so the "
"emulator works unchanged, but accounts, achievements and progress are "
"separate: log in with your RetroPlatinas account."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:50
msgid "Can I use another emulator?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/faq.html:51
msgid ""
"Today DuckStation is the only emulator we test. Others built on rcheevos may "
"work if they let you change the server address, but they are not supported."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/getting-started.html:4
msgid ""
"RetroPlatinas works with an unmodified DuckStation: point it at this site, "
"log in and play."
msgstr ""

