#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:4
msgid ""
"Besides achievements, a game can have leaderboards, which rank scores and "
"times, and a rich presence script, which tells others what you are doing in "
"the game."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:10
msgid ""
"A leaderboard starts when its start condition becomes true, is cancelled by "
"its cancel condition and submits the value it tracks when its submit "
"condition becomes true. The emulator shows the running value while it is "
"active."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:11
msgid ""
"Leaderboards only run in hardcore mode: in softcore the emulator neither "
"tracks nor submits them."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:12
msgid ""
"Each player keeps one entry, their best: the highest score, or the lowest "
"value when lower is better, as with times. A worse attempt does not replace "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:13
msgid ""
"The game page's Leaderboards tab lists them; each has its own page with "
"every rank."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:14
msgid ""
"Staff add new leaderboards. To propose one, describe it in the game page's "
"comments."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:16
msgid ""
"A leaderboard is written as four condition strings, the same syntax as "
"achievements:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:18
msgid "Leaderboards in the RetroAchievements docs"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:22
msgid "Rich presence"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:24
msgid ""
"While you play, the emulator reads a few memory values and sends a short "
"line about what you are doing, such as the level you are in. The site shows "
"it as playing now on your profile and on the home page."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:25
msgid ""
"The emulator sends it about every two minutes, and only fetches the script "
"when a game loads, so a change shows after the game is opened again."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:26
msgid ""
"Each game has one script, which staff maintain. Without one, the site only "
"shows which game you are playing."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:28
msgid ""
"A script defines formats and lookups, then the line to display, reading "
"memory with macros:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/leaderboards-and-rich-presence.html:34
msgid "Rich presence in the RetroAchievements docs"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:4
msgid ""
"Every achievement is official or unofficial: its status decides whether "
"unlocking it is recorded and worth points. Sets grow from players writing, "
"testing and reviewing them."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:8
msgid "Statuses"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:12
msgid ""
"Every player receives it as an official achievement, and unlocking it is "
"recorded and worth its points. Only official achievements count towards "
"rankings, completion and platinums."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:16
msgid ""
"Every player receives it too, in the emulator's unofficial list with Test "
"Unofficial Achievements on, and the game page lists it in its own section. "
"It is never recorded and never worth points. A new achievement starts "
"unofficial."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:22
msgid "Who changes a status"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:24
msgid ""
"The author or staff make an achievement official or unofficial in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:25
msgid ""
"Making an official achievement unofficial keeps everyone's unlocks but takes "
"its points out of their totals; making it official again counts them again."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:30 templates/home.html:87
msgid "How to contribute"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:33
msgid "Read the code notes"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:34
msgid ""
"Each game page links its code notes: what the community found at each memory "
"address."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:37
msgid "Write and test it unofficial"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:38
msgid ""
"Follow the creating achievements guide, and test it in the game before "
"making it official."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:39
msgid "Creating achievements →"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:43
msgid ""
"Once it fires at the right moment, make it official. Players can leave "
"feedback in the comments on its page."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:46
msgid "Share what you found"
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:47
msgid ""
"Add a code note for every address you worked out, so the next author starts "
"from it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:55
msgid ""
"A code note describes one memory address of a game: its size, the values it "
"takes and what they mean."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:56
msgid ""
"Anyone can read and search them. A logged-in player adds new ones; the "
"author or staff edit or delete a note."
msgstr ""

#: templates/docs/statuses-and-contributing.html:57
msgid ""
"Notes are a starting point, not the truth: many come from RetroAchievements "
"and describe another region or revision of the game. Check each address in "
"the game before relying on it."
msgstr ""

